WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.863 --> 00:00:04.985
Line 3 has to stand in hall B before the summer shutdown ends.

2
00:00:05.691 --> 00:00:10.509
The work is about power, a switchboard and a PLC that controls the line.

3
00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:14.150
You are not an electrician and not a programmer.

4
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:18.872
The installer and the PLC programmer know far more about it than you.

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:21.458
Yet you lead this project.

6
00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:23.114
How do you do that?

7
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.471
We follow it through the four topics of the module.

8
00:00:27.784 --> 00:00:29.572
The first topic is the mindset.

9
00:00:30.361 --> 00:00:35.528
The installer is the subject matter expert, and he knows how the connection works.

10
00:00:36.511 --> 00:00:39.564
See yourself as a director, not as an expert.

11
00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:43.306
You own the route, the expert owns the engine.

12
00:00:44.058 --> 00:00:48.621
You make sure the right person answers each technical question, by a date.

13
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.606
What the project delivers you decide with the sponsor.

14
00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.810
How it is built is up to the installer.

15
00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:59.202
For the mindset we use a naive question.

16
00:01:00.513 --> 00:01:02.870
The second topic is asking questions.

17
00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:08.346
You cannot judge the answers, so the quality of your questions is your expertise.

18
00:01:09.364 --> 00:01:12.859
Ask the installer what is explicitly not in the connection.

19
00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.718
That is where the misunderstandings are.

20
00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:19.359
He assumes the power cabinet is big enough.

21
00:01:20.114 --> 00:01:24.190
Write that down, because an assumption is a risk until it is checked.

22
00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:28.866
For asking questions we use a question set and a premortem.

23
00:01:30.187 --> 00:01:32.660
The third topic is working with experts.

24
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.619
The installer says the power cabinet is big enough.

25
00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:40.153
You trust his skill and check the result.

26
00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:43.812
Who checked the calculation, and where is it signed?

27
00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:49.078
Every important piece of work is checked by a second qualified person.

28
00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.623
You make sure he is there, you are not him yourself.

29
00:01:53.615 --> 00:01:57.214
But the PLC programmer finds the power cabinet too small.

30
00:01:57.889 --> 00:02:01.814
Two experts, two opinions, and you cannot judge the content.

31
00:02:02.886 --> 00:02:06.183
With experts we use a spot check and a second opinion.

32
00:02:07.485 --> 00:02:09.946
The fourth topic is steering and deciding.

33
00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:13.936
The installer says the connection is ninety percent done.

34
00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:19.368
Outside your field a percentage is the weakest measure, because it is an opinion.

35
00:02:20.063 --> 00:02:25.021
Count milestones instead, which are yes or no, like the switchboard energised.

36
00:02:26.053 --> 00:02:28.956
Only count a milestone when the evidence exists,

37
00:02:29.071 --> 00:02:31.556
such as a signed test report or a demo.

38
00:02:32.264 --> 00:02:34.899
That way the sponsor decides on facts.

39
00:02:35.895 --> 00:02:37.787
A supplier builds the switchboard.

40
00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:42.266
We test it there before shipping, with a factory acceptance test.

41
00:02:43.622 --> 00:02:44.481
It connects.

42
00:02:45.196 --> 00:02:47.924
You are the director, you ask good questions,

43
00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:50.827
and you trust experts but check what counts.

44
00:02:51.532 --> 00:02:52.937
You steer on evidence.

45
00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.833
The second checker recalculates and signs.

46
00:02:57.533 --> 00:03:02.502
The power cabinet is too small, gets bigger, and line 3 gets into place.

47
00:03:03.827 --> 00:03:05.452
This is the map of Projects.

48
00:03:06.181 --> 00:03:11.591
Leading projects outside your field is the fourth station of People and influence.

49
00:03:12.643 --> 00:03:15.790
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

50
00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:19.327
Start with the mindset, at Basics level.

51
00:03:20.377 --> 00:03:24.104
At Working knowledge you add curiosity, single point of failure,

52
00:03:24.243 --> 00:03:26.693
decision criteria and one-way doors.

53
00:03:27.702 --> 00:03:29.862
At Advanced you add the trust equation,

54
00:03:30.024 --> 00:03:33.809
reference classes, context switching and the pyramid principle.

55
00:03:34.828 --> 00:03:37.150
At Expert you add what you never hand over,

56
00:03:37.289 --> 00:03:40.180
teach-back, the watermelon status and shadowing.

57
00:03:41.206 --> 00:03:45.270
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
